      "id": "sg1v6pv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Natural Vegetation"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Tropical Evergreen Forests thrive in regions with high humidity and over 200 cm of annual rainfall, keeping their leaves year-round.",
        "Tropical Deciduous Forests are the most widespread forest type in India, often called Monsoon Forests, and shed leaves in dry summers.",
        "Thorn Forests and scrubs develop in semi-arid regions with less than 70 cm of rainfall, featuring deep-rooted and succulent vegetation.",
        "Mountain Forests show a distinct vertical zonation of vegetation types ranging from wet temperate to alpine grasslands as altitude increases.",
        "Mangrove Forests grow along mudflats and coastal deltas affected by tides, with specialized stilt root systems adaptable to saline waters."
      ],
      "id": "e3hr044"
    },
